From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 19:11:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(render): animate native moving piston blocks

Create a Java moving piston block entity when translated native piston data arrives for the matching moving-piston state. Java 26.3 MovingPistonBlock.newBlockEntity returns null and ClientPacketListener.handleBlockEntityData only loads an existing entity, so remote translated piston updates previously disappeared without animation. Native server actor pushes remain authoritative; suppress Java local moving-piston entity pushes in Bedrock sessions to avoid duplication. Retain normal Java behavior outside Bedrock sessions.
---
 .../block/MixinBedrockMovingPistonBlock.java  | 30 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../MixinBedrockPistonMovingBlockEntity.java  | 28 +++++++++++++++++
 .../viafabricplus-bedrock.mixins.json         |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 60 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/block/MixinBedrockMovingPistonBlock.java
 create mode 100644 src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/block/MixinBedrockPistonMovingBlockEntity.java

diff --git a/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/block/MixinBedrockMovingPistonBlock.java b/src/main/java/com/viaversion/viafabricplus/bedrock/injection/mixin/features/block/MixinBedrockMovingPistonBlock.java
